<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stockholm Bloodbath</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1520</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a> Bloodbath was the mass execution of some eighty Swedish nobles, clergy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> in Stockholm in November 1520, ordered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-ii-of-denmark">Christian II of Denmark</a> after his conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Accused of heresy for opposing the archbishop, they were beheaded in the main square. The killings provoked a rebellion led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-i-of-sweden">Gustav Vasa</a>, who became king of Sweden in 1523, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stockholm-bloodbath.jpg" alt="Stockholm Bloodbath" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blodbadstavlan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
